## 1. Isolated Test Data & Forbidden Commands (`E5`)

- **Isolation strategy**: `{{isolation_strategy}}` (e.g., dedicated tenant/workspace per test run, run-ID prefixes, or disposable local database fixtures).
- **Local seed command**: `{{seed_cmd}}` (executes against local/disposable storage only).
- **Forbidden data commands**: **never** run `{{forbidden_data_commands}}` — they clone, reset, or overwrite shared business data. Never use production data or production database snapshots.

## 2. Per-Role Test Accounts & Secret Hygiene (`E6`, `E13`)

| Role | Target Environment | Account Identifier (Name Only) | Config / Env Key Reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| `{{role_name}}` | `{{env_name}}` | `{{account_identifier}}` | `{{config_key_ref}}` |

- Load credentials exclusively from `{{credentials_source}}` (local, git-ignored config).
- **Secret hygiene (`E13`)**: never echo, log, or paste passwords, tokens, or API keys into terminal output, test logs, or the environment record. Never test with real user accounts.

## 3. External Providers: Sandboxes vs. Labelled Stubs (`E7`)

| External Provider | Preferred Sandbox | Network-Edge Stub (Tool & Spec) | Required Scenarios | Config Switch |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `{{provider_name}}` | `{{sandbox_mode}}` | `{{stub_tool_and_file}}` | `success` · `4xx` · `401/403` · `5xx` · `timeout` · `malformed` | `{{provider_switch_env}}` |

- **Order of preference**: (1) provider sandbox/test mode, (2) network-edge stub configured via URL/env override without changing application code, (3) report **`BLOCKED`** if neither exists.
- **Mandatory labelling**: every test case executed against a stub must record `stubbed: <provider>` in the evidence (`[03]({{ref_03}})`), and state which integration cases still require verification against the live provider sandbox.

